"Help Center Desktop (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-wish-list)\nciteturn1000view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":13}); Redirected to URL: https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-wish-list?language=en_US; Total lines: 7\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: CSS Error\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nView accompanying PDF (https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-accompanying-pdf)\nciteturn1000view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":14}); Total lines: 111\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Ask A Question Library Listening Player Troubleshooting\nL13: ## View accompanying PDF\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: View accompanying PDF\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: view-accompanying-pdf\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You can check if an audiobook includes a PDF by looking at the title's detail page on Audible. If a PDF is included, this will be indicated.\nL29: \nL30: You can view the PDFs through either the Audible app or desktop site.\nL31: \nL32: Note:\nL33:   * When you purchase a title, the accompanying PDF will be available in your Audible Library along with the audio.\nL34:   * If the PDF doesn't appear in your library, but the audio mentions an accompanying file, please contact the 【1†Audible Customer Service team†www.audible.com】.\nL35: \nL36: In this article:\nL37: \nL38:   * 【2†How do I see the accompanying PDF in the Audible app?】\nL39:   * 【3†How do I see the accompanying PDF from the Audible site?】\nL40: ## How do I see the accompanying PDF in the Audible app?\nL41: \nL42:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL43:   2. Go to your Library.\nL44:   3. Select an audiobook that has an accompanying PDF.\nL45:   4. Select the PDF button.\nL46: \nL47: Note: For Android devices, once the PDF has opened, you’ll have the option to save it to your device.\nL48: ## How do I see the accompanying PDF from the Audible site?\nL49: \nL50:   1. Go to the Audible site.\nL51:   2. Select Library.\nL52:   3. Find the title with the PDF.\nL53:   4. Select View PDF.\nL54: \nL55: Note: Once you select View PDF, the file will automatically download to your computer.\nL56: \nL57: Did this answer your question?\nL58: \nL59: 【4†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL60: \nL61: \nL62: \nL63: 【5†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL64: \nL65:  Back to top\nL66: \nL67: 【6†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL68: \nL69: 【7†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL70: ## Need more assistance?\nL71: \nL72: 【8†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL73: \nL74: \nL75: \nL76: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL77: \nL78: \nL79: \nL80: Worst\nL81: \nL82: 1\nL83: \nL84: 2\nL85: \nL86: 3\nL87: \nL88: 4\nL89: \nL90: 5\nL91: \nL92: 6\nL93: \nL94: 7\nL95: \nL96: Best\nL97: \nL98: \nL99: \nL100: Region\nL101: \nL102: United States\nL103: \nL104: Language\nL105: \nL106: English\nL107: \nL108: Loading\nL109: \nL110: View accompanying PDF 【9†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage Listening reminders (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-listening-reminders)\nciteturn1000view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":26}); Total lines: 151\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: This page has an error. You might just need to refresh it. [Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'bind')]\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: App settings Ask A Question Getting started Listening+3\nL13: ## Manage Listening reminders\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Manage Listening reminders\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: manage-listening-reminders\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Listening reminders help you maintain a consistent listening schedule by sending notifications at times you choose. You can set up reminders through your app settings or while listening to an audiobook.\nL29: \nL30: Note: Reminders are currently only available for audiobooks, not podcasts.\nL31: \nL32: In this article:\nL33:   * 【1†How do I create a Listening reminder?】\nL34:   * 【2†How do I edit a Listening reminder?】\nL35:   * 【3†How do I delete a Listening reminder?】\nL36: ## How do I create a Listening reminder?\nL37: \nL38: You can create a Listening reminder from your app settings or from your player screen.\nL39: \nL40: Create from the player screen\nL41: \nL42:   1. Open the player screen.\nL43:   2. Select the 3-dot More menu at the top of the player.\nL44:   3. Select Listening reminders.\nL45:   4. Allow notifications if prompted.\nL46:   5. Select your preferred days.\nL47:   6. Select your preferred time.\nL48:   7. Select Save.\nL49: \nL50: Create from the app settings\nL51:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL52:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL53:   3. Select Listening reminders.\nL54:   4. Select Create.\nL55:   5. Select Pick a listen and choose your audiobook.\nL56:   6. Select your preferred days.\nL57:   7. Select your preferred time.\nL58:   8. Select Save.\nL59: ## How do I edit a Listening reminder?\nL60: \nL61: Edit from the player screen\nL62: \nL63:   1. Open the player screen.\nL64:   2. Select the 3-dot More menu at the top of the player.\nL65:   3. Select Listening reminders.\nL66:   4. Make the changes needed.\nL67:   5. Select Save.\nL68: \nL69: Edit from the app settings\nL70: \nL71:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL72:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL73:   3. Select Listening reminders.\nL74:   4. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL75:   5. Select Edit reminder.\nL76:   6. Make any changes you need.\nL77:   7. Select Save.\nL78: ## How do I delete a Listening reminder?\nL79: \nL80: Delete from the player screen\nL81: \nL82:   1. Open the player screen.\nL83:   2. Select the 3-dot More menu at the top of the player.\nL84:   3. Select Listening reminders.\nL85:   4. Select Delete at the bottom of the screen.\nL86:   5. Confirm by selecting Delete reminder.\nL87: \nL88: Delete from the app settings\nL89:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL90:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL91:   3. Select Listening reminders.\nL92:   4. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL93:   5. Select Delete at the bottom of the screen.\nL94:   6. Confirm by selecting Delete reminder.\nL95: \nL96: Note: You'll need to 【4†enable notifications】 for the Audible app in your device settings to receive reminders.\nL97: \nL98: Did this answer your question?\nL99: \nL100: 【5†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL101: \nL102: \nL103: \nL104: 【6†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL105: \nL106:  Back to top\nL107: \nL108: 【7†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL109: 【8†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL110: ## Need more assistance?\nL111: \nL112: 【9†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL113: \nL114: \nL115: \nL116: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL117: \nL118: \nL119: \nL120: Worst\nL121: \nL122: 1\nL123: \nL124: 2\nL125: \nL126: 3\nL127: \nL128: 4\nL129: \nL130: 5\nL131: \nL132: 6\nL133: \nL134: 7\nL135: \nL136: Best\nL137: \nL138: \nL139: \nL140: Region\nL141: \nL142: United States\nL143: \nL144: Language\nL145: \nL146: English\nL147: \nL148: Loading\nL149: \nL150: Manage Listening reminders 【10†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLearn about Audible listening challenges (https://help.audible.com/s/article/audible-listening-challenge)\nciteturn1000view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":27}); Total lines: 136\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Listening Player Player tools\nL13: ## Learn about Audible listening challenges\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Learn about Audible listening challenges\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: audible-listening-challenge\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Listening challenges are a fun way to build your daily listening habit. Set a daily goal and track your progress to earn achievement badges.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【1†How do I join a challenge?】\nL32:   * 【2†How do I track my progress?】\nL33:   * 【3†How can I invite others to join the challenge with me?】\nL34:   * 【4†What do I receive for completing a challenge?】\nL35:   * 【5†What happens if I cancel while participating in a listening challenge?】\nL36: ## How do I join a challenge?\nL37: \nL38:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL39:   2. Swipe down until you find \"Start a listening habit.\"\nL40:   3. Select Join a Challenge.\nL41:   4. Pick a challenge goal:\nL42: \nL43:   * Daily listening challenge: 10, 20, or 30 minutes.\nL44:   * Multi-title listening challenge: 3, 4, or 5 titles.\nL45: \nL46:   1. Select Commit to my goal.\nL47: \nL48: Notes:\nL49:   * You cannot change your goal after you start. Each challenge can only be taken once — watch for new challenges in the future.\nL50:   * You don't need to start a new audiobook to participate in the multi-title listening challenge. Continue listening to your current audiobook and your progress will appear on the progress screen.\nL51: ## How do I track my progress?\nL52: \nL53: Your listening is tracked automatically when you start the challenge. For the daily listening challenge, progress updates at the end of your listening session. For the multi-title listening challenge, progress updates each time you finish a title.\nL54: \nL55: From the Home tab\nL56: \nL57:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL58:   2. Select the See Progress button.\nL59: \nL60: From your Profile\nL61: \nL62:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL63:   2. Go to your Profile.\nL64:   3. Swipe to \"Elevate your listening habit.\"\nL65:   4. Select See Progress.\nL66: Notes:\nL67: \nL68:   * Refresh the app to see your updated listening minutes.\nL69:   * Any audiobook you finish counts toward your multi-title goal. Audiobooks from non-US marketplaces and podcasts don't count toward this goal.\nL70:   * If your challenge is not recording your progress, please contact 【6†Audible Customer Support†www.audible.com】 for assistance.\nL71: ## How can I invite others to join the challenge with me?\nL72: \nL73: When you select Invite others, you can let your friends know about the challenge and how to sign up. You can also share links to the daily listening challenge or multi-title listening challenge directly with your friends.\nL74: \nL75: ## What do I receive for completing a challenge?\nL76: \nL77: You will receive an achievement badge that's permanently added to the Badges section of your Audible app. You can view and share your achievement anytime.\nL78: ## What happens if I cancel while participating in a listening challenge?\nL79: \nL80: If you cancel your membership, you'll lose any challenge progress and you won't be able to restart the challenge.\nL81: \nL82: Did this answer your question?\nL83: \nL84: 【7†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL85: \nL86: \nL87: \nL88: 【8†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL89: \nL90:  Back to top\nL91: \nL92: 【9†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL93: \nL94: 【10†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL95: ## Need more assistance?\nL96: \nL97: 【11†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL98: \nL99: \nL100: \nL101: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL102: \nL103: \nL104: \nL105: Worst\nL106: \nL107: 1\nL108: \nL109: 2\nL110: \n